<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine unemployment rises to 257,665 in September.</title>
<headline>Ukraine unemployment rises to 257,665 in September.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Registered unemployment in Ukraine rose slightly to 257,665 at the end of September from 242,090 at the end of August, the Statistics Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It gave the following data:</p>
<p> UKRAINIAN UNEMPLOYMENT	SEPT 96    AUG 96   SEPT 95</p>
<p> number of unemployed	  257,665    242,090  133,926</p>
<p>NOTE - Official Ukrainian information tends to understate</p>
<p>unemployment levels.</p>
<p>The Labour Ministry said earlier in the week that registered unemployment stood at about 0.9 percent of the work force.</p>
<p>Labour Minister Mykola Biloblodsky said real unemployment stood at about 3.5 million. Ukraine has a population of about 51 million people.</p>
<p>The Labour Ministry forecasts registered unemployment will rise to 1.3 million by the end of next year.</p>
<p>--Yuri Kulikov, Kiev newsroom, +380 44 229 2264</p>
